uestion-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine2/raw/openstax-heart.json"]}, {"group": "note0", "literal": "У рыб сердце имеет две камеры: предсердие и желудочек.", "literalSHA256": "0a04f4c8f755216529a36c7de3d3cde6a1ff9bc8e6ef9790396436f417d2416e", "primaryGround": "The note says fish have one atrium and one ventricle, matching the source description of their two-chambered heart and the roles of those chambers.", "locator": "OpenStax Biology 2e 40.1 L46, L53", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine2/raw/openstax-biology-circulation.json"]}, {"group": "note1", "literal": "Межпредсердная перегородка разделяет предсердия, а межжелудочковая — желудочки.", "literalSHA256": "0e539731a0ebfba45688658acc9fba958df57f94ebe258db26dba48fcde48e3d", "primaryGround": "The note names the interatrial septum between atria and interventricular septum between ventricles, both stated in the anatomy passage.", "locator": "OpenStax A&P 2e Heart Anatomy L106-L108", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine2/raw/openstax-heart.json"]}, {"group": "note2", "literal": "Сердце большинства земноводных имеет три камеры: два предсердия и один желудочек.", "literalSHA256": "29202e15d79d7cf3bb900f3a394273ccf8b1920055127220aca37420471e28f5", "primaryGround": "The source states that amphibians have two atria and one ventricle, and describes the resulting three-chambered heart.", "locator": "OpenStax Biology 2e 40.1 L47, L56", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine2/raw/openstax-biology-circulation.json"]}, {"group": "note3", "literal": "Клапаны расположены в отверстиях между камерами и на выходах к лёгочному стволу и аорте; они направляют кровь в одну сторону.", "literalSHA256": "b55fdcbb8ab589692652bf19c97c1882b569bb7ca15d68fe686b36f9754b3805", "primaryGround": "The source places valves in openings between atria and ventricles and at the exits to the pulmonary trunk and aorta, and states that valves ensure one-way blood flow.", "locator": "OpenStax A&P 2e Heart Anatomy L109-L110", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine2/raw/openstax-heart.json"]}], "fourFullPromptAnswerNoteAssessments": [{"slot": 0, "fullPrompt": "Сколько камер у сердца человека?", "answer": "Две", "note": "У рыб сердце имеет две камеры: предсердие и желудочек.", "grammar": "The answer is a standalone short numeral response to “Сколько камер”; all four alternatives use the same grammatical form and category.", "plausibilityUniqueKeyAndNoteTruth

